# PrimeVue Local Component Imports

## Critical: Local Imports Only

PrimeVue components should be **locally imported** in each Vue file that uses them. Do NOT globally register components in `main.ts`.

## Component Import Pattern

**❌ WRONG - Global registration in main.ts:**

```typescript
// main.ts
import Button from 'primevue/button'
import Dialog from 'primevue/dialog'
import DataTable from 'primevue/datatable'

app.component('Button', Button)
app.component('Dialog', Dialog)
app.component('DataTable', DataTable)
```

**✅ CORRECT - Local imports in each component:**

```vue
<template>
  <Dialog v-model:visible="showDialog">
    <DataTable :value="items">
      <!-- columns -->
    </DataTable>
    <Button label="Close" @click="showDialog = false" />
  </Dialog>
</template>

<script setup lang="ts">
import Button from 'primevue/button'
import Dialog from 'primevue/dialog'
import DataTable from 'primevue/datatable'
import Column from 'primevue/column'

const showDialog = ref(false)
const items = ref([])
</script>
```

## Common PrimeVue Imports

```typescript
// Buttons
import Button from 'primevue/button'

// Form Components
import InputText from 'primevue/inputtext'
import Dropdown from 'primevue/dropdown'
import Calendar from 'primevue/calendar'
import Checkbox from 'primevue/checkbox'
import InputNumber from 'primevue/inputnumber'
import Textarea from 'primevue/textarea'

// Data Display
import DataTable from 'primevue/datatable'
import Column from 'primevue/column'
import Card from 'primevue/card'
import Tag from 'primevue/tag'

// Overlays
import Dialog from 'primevue/dialog'
import ConfirmDialog from 'primevue/confirmdialog'
import Toast from 'primevue/toast'

// Navigation
import TabView from 'primevue/tabview'
import TabPanel from 'primevue/tabpanel'
import Menu from 'primevue/menu'

// Feedback
import ProgressBar from 'primevue/progressbar'
import Skeleton from 'primevue/skeleton'
```

## Why Local Imports?

1. **Tree-shaking** - Only imports what's used, reducing bundle size
2. **Explicit Dependencies** - Clear which components are used in each file
3. **Better IDE Support** - Autocomplete and type checking work correctly
4. **Maintainability** - Easy to track component usage across the codebase

## Import Organization

Organize imports in this order:

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
// 1. Vue core
import { ref, computed, watch } from 'vue'

// 2. Vue Router
import { useRoute, useRouter } from 'vue-router'

// 3. PrimeVue components
import Button from 'primevue/button'
import Dialog from 'primevue/dialog'
import DataTable from 'primevue/datatable'

// 4. PrimeVue composables
import { useToast } from 'primevue/usetoast'
import { useConfirm } from 'primevue/useconfirm'

// 5. Local stores (relative paths)
import { useProjectsStore } from '../stores/projects'

// 6. Local types (relative paths)
import type { Project } from '../types/project'

// 7. Local components (relative paths)
import MyComponent from './MyComponent.vue'
</script>
```

## Best Practices

1. **Import only what you use** - Don't import unused components
2. **Use consistent naming** - Import name should match component name
3. **Group related imports** - Keep PrimeVue imports together
4. **Remember sub-components** - DataTable needs Column, TabView needs TabPanel
